# Pages generated by cmd/bandsplit embed the SOURCE RECORDING. This repository is public and
# other people's material must never enter it (umbrella CLAUDE.md §4). The tool now refuses to
# write without an explicit -out; this is the second net.
*.html

# Scraped third-party material and its fetcher must never enter this repo.
# Their home is reference/ (outside every git repo) — see the umbrella CLAUDE.md section 4.
#
# WHAT WAS HERE, and what is still reachable. Two different things were committed on
# 2026-06-17 (450367f) and removed on 2026-09-10 (9d7d380) — a 12-week window in a
# public repository:
#
#   (1) _blogtmp/ — 15 AtariAge blog posts as verbatim text, 39,582 B. Other people's
#       writing. This is the licensing problem, and the reason reference/ sits outside
#       every git repo in the first place.
#   (2) _blog_fetch.py — 47 lines. Not other people's writing, so (1)'s wording does not
#       cover it: line 4 read `open("../reference/atariage/aa_cookie.txt")`, and the file
#       fetched through curl_cffi with a spoofed Chrome User-Agent.
#
# The history was deliberately NOT rewritten (decision 2026-09-10). `git show
# 450367f:_blog_fetch.py` still prints both the cookie path and the technique, and it
# always will. The reasoning: the blog text is public AtariAge material rather than a
# secret; the cookie value itself was never committed (measured: zero hits across all
# refs); the path names a file on one laptop and is useless elsewhere; and rewriting
# every hash would disrupt the sessions sharing this working tree while leaving any
# existing clone untouched anyway.
#
# It would also not have achieved much: the same technique is described in CHANGELOG.md
# around line 8657 ("direct AtariAge fetch via curl_cffi (Cloudflare bypass)", "the
# browser Cookie header incl. cf_clearance"), which is a change record and stays.
#
# This paragraph exists because the removal alone reads as concealment. Choosing to
# leave something and forgetting it look identical from outside; only the note tells
# them apart.
_blogtmp/
_blog_fetch.py
aa_cookie*.txt
